[
  "ACT 1: COLD OPEN & PERSONAL GROUNDING [00:00 - 03:00]\nScene: 01. Starting Soon -> 02. Monologue / Full Camera\n\nWelcome back to The Sound Above. I am Mike Hall. Today we enter The Architecture & Testing Discipline. Before code synthesis models and automated agents, developers in Chicago were building grassroots rooms to escape corporate silos. Today we rewatch Episode 27: Rich Hickey from GOTO Chicago / UGtastic Archive (2012).",
  "ACT 2: SETTING THE HISTORICAL SCENE [03:00 - 08:00]\nScene: 02. Monologue / Full Camera\n\nRich Hickey's talks and Clojure philosophy electrified Chicago craftsmanship groups, prompting practitioners to question mutability and object-oriented complexity. When we recorded this in 2012, there were no corporate sponsor filters. Developers were meeting after hours, sharing hard-won lessons on deliberate practice and system boundaries.",
  "ACT 3: THE CORE INQUIRY: THE SOUND ABOVE [08:00 - 14:00]\nScene: 02. Monologue / Full Camera -> 04. Split Screen\n\nWhat led Rich Hickey to spend two years in self-funded isolation designing Clojure? What is the profound difference between 'simple' and 'easy'? Who inspired Rich Hickey before they stepped onto this stage? What records were playing in the background when this movement formed?",
  "ACT 4: HALLWAY REWATCH & VIDEO REACTION [14:00 - 28:00]\nScene: 03. Reaction - Video Focus\n\nRoll archive footage (YouTube ID: HF0ZsbUjEDw). Watch for the unvarnished hallway exchanges, the emphasis on craft over speed, and the sheer enthusiasm of engineers taking responsibility for their software.",
  "ACT 5: THE AI-ERA PARALLEL & TERMINAL WORKBENCH [28:00 - 40:00]\nScene: 05. Workbench - Code & Terminal\n\nSimplicity is an objective quality: unbraiding concerns. Easy is familiar. AI makes complex things easy to generate, making intentional simplicity vital. When implementation is cheap, verification and clarity become everything. We cannot accept the mirage of competence. Let us examine the terminal contracts directly.",
  "ACT 6: COMMUNITY CODA, OUTRO & NEXT STREAM [40:00 - 45:00]\nScene: 08. Outro & Next Stream\n\nThank you for joining today's session. Full transcripts, provenance notes, and companion research are available at just3ws.com. In our next broadcast, we explore Episode 28. Until next time, keep your feedback loops fast and your code humane."
]